>> servings: 4
>> source: https://www.jamieoliver.com/recipes/vegetables/classic-ratatouille/

Prep your ingredients before you start – peel and cut the @red onions{2} into wedges, then peel and finely slice the @garlic{4%clove}. Trim the @aubergines{2} and @courgettes{3}, deseed the @peppers{3} and chop into 2.5cm chunks. Roughly chop the @tomatoes{6} . Pick the @basil{1/2%bunch} leaves and set aside, then finely slice the stalks.

Heat @olive oil{2%tbsp} in a large #casserole pan{} over a medium heat, add the chopped aubergines, courgettes and peppers (you may need to do this in batches) and fry for around ~{5%minutes}, or until golden and softened, but not cooked through. Spoon the cooked veg into a #large bowl{}.

To the pan, add the onion, garlic, basil stalks and @thyme{} leaves with another drizzle of oil, if needed. Fry for ~{10 to 15%minutes}, or until softened and golden.

Return the cooked veg to the pan and stir in the fresh and @tinned tomatoes{400%g}, the @balsamic vinegar{1%tbsp} and a good pinch of @sea salt{} and @black pepper{}.

Mix well, breaking up the tomatoes with the back of a spoon. Cover the pan and simmer over a low heat for ~{30%minutes}, or until reduced, sticky and sweet.

Tear in the basil leaves, finely grate in the @lemon{1/2} zest and adjust the seasoning, if needed. Serve with a hunk of bread or steamed rice.
